<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Achalm</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Achalm is a hill of 707 metres on the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-jura">Swabian Jura</a> above Reutlingen in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>. A castle built on it in the 11th century was the seat of the counts of Achalm, who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwiefalten">Zwiefalten</a> Abbey in 1089, and it later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> and then to Württemberg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/achalm.jpg" alt="Achalm" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alupus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blick_auf_die_Achalm_von_den_Pfullinger_Streuobstwiesen_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
